<meta title="Counting Elephants" />

Aerial transects and ground counts are the two standard survey methods for
savanna elephants.

## Aerial Transects

Aerial transects remain the standard method: a light aircraft flies parallel
lines and observers count animals in a fixed-width strip on each side.

## Ground Counts

Ground counts complement the aerial survey at known aggregation points such as
waterholes during the dry season.
